.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt SSG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssg
.Nd build a static site of HTML, markdown and plain-text pages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm build
.Op Fl \-drafts
.Op Fl \-check-links
.Op Fl \-target Ar name
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar content-dir
.Nm
.Cm init | serve | watch | check | list | clean | doctor
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dir
.Nm
.Cm new
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm plugins list
.Nm
.Cm plugins meta
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm completions
.Ar bash | zsh | fish
.Nm
.Cm render
.Op Fl \-strict
.Op Fl \-text
.Op Fl \-no-html
.Op Fl \-scripts | \-no-scripts
.Op Fl \-no-extensions
.Ar file | Fl
.Nm
.Fl \-help | \-version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
In its first form,
.Nm
builds the site in
.Ar content-dir ,
which must contain a
.Pa site.toml .
Every markdown page becomes three files in the dist directory:
.Pa .html
(the page in the HTML skeleton),
.Pa .md
(templates resolved, frontmatter removed) and
.Pa .txt
(wrapped plain text).
Every other file is copied as is.
The content directory format, templates and output layout are described in
.Xr ssg 5 .
.Pp
A build runs in this order:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
Read
.Pa site.toml .
Relative paths in it are relative to
.Ar content-dir .
.It
Refuse an unsafe dist directory (see
.Sx DIAGNOSTICS ) .
Nothing is written before this check.
.It
Load and check the skeleton.
.It
Walk
.Ar content-dir
top-down, in byte order of file names.
Files ending in
.Pa .md
(case-sensitive) are pages; other regular files are assets.
Skipped: names starting with
.Sq \&.
(except directories named
.Pa .well-known ) ,
the dist and templates directories, the skeleton,
.Pa site.toml
at the top level, paths matched by
.Pa .assetignore
files or the
.Ic ignore
key, directories that contain a
.Pa .git
entry (unless
.Ic nested_repos
is true), and the contents of symbolic links to directories.
.It
Empty the dist directory if
.Ic clean
is true and
.Nm
created it (it holds a
.Pa .ssg-dist
marker).
.It
Copy assets.
.It
Render pages: a first pass over all pages to resolve frontmatter and templates, then the
real render with navigation keys
.Pq Ic children , parent_* , prev_* , next_*
filled in.
.It
Write
.Pa sitemap.xml
if
.Ic base_url
is set.
.It
With
.Fl \-check-links ,
check local links.
.It
Print a summary line to standard error.
.El
.Pp
An error stops the build at once.
Assets and pages written before it stay in dist.
.Pp
In its second form,
.Nm
.Cm render
converts one markdown
.Ar file ,
or standard input when the argument is
.Fl ,
to HTML (or text) on standard output.
Frontmatter is not parsed, templates are not evaluated and
.Pa site.toml
is not read: a
.Li ---
block renders as markdown.
Options are the built-in defaults: raw HTML on and allow-listed, extensions,
heading ids and bare autolinks on, text wrapped at 80 columns.
.Ss Commands
The first argument is a command only if it is one of the names below; anything else is the
legacy form, and
.Nm
.Ar dir
means
.Nm
.Cm build
.Ar dir
throughout 1.x.
A directory with a command's name is written
.Pa ./list .
.Ar dir
defaults to the current directory, and options go after the command.
.Bl -tag -width "completions"
.It Cm build
Build the site, as described above.
.It Cm init
Create
.Ar dir
with
.Pa site.toml , skeleton.html , templates/base.md , index.md
and a
.Pa .gitignore
holding
.Pa dist/ .
Refuses if any of them exists.
.It Cm new Ar path
Write
.Ar path Ns Pa .md
with
.Ic title
(from the file name) and
.Ic date
(today, or from
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH )
frontmatter.
Refuses an existing file, an absolute path and any path containing
.Pa .. .
.It Cm serve
Build, serve dist on 127.0.0.1 and rebuild when a file changes.
Open pages reload themselves.
Misses get the
.Pa /404/
page or
.Pa 404.html
with status 404.
Takes
.Fl \-port Ar n
(default 8000, 0 for any free port),
.Fl \-open
and
.Fl \-drafts .
.It Cm watch
Build, then rebuild when a file changes.
.It Cm check
Build into a scratch directory and report what
.Fl \-check-links
reports, plus pages nothing links to, images without alt text and
.Li {{keys}}
that nothing defines.
Findings are warnings, so the exit status is 0 unless
.Fl \-fail-on-warning
is given.
.It Cm list
Print each page's URL and source file, sorted by URL.
.It Cm clean
Empty dist, but only if it is missing, empty or holds the
.Pa .ssg-dist
marker.
.It Cm doctor
Check the config, dist, templates, skeleton and plugin tables, and warn when
.Pa dist/.ssg-dist
would be deployed because no
.Pa .assetsignore ,
.Pa .vercelignore
or
.Pa vercel.json
names it.
Exit 1 if any check is an error.
.It Cm plugins list
List the
.Sy [plugin.name]
tables in file order, each with its version and path, or why it cannot be used.
.It Cm plugins meta Ar name
Run the plugin's
.Fl \-meta
and print the JSON object it returns on one line.
Exit 1 if there is no such table or the plugin cannot be run.
.It Cm completions Ar shell
Print a completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
.El
.Ss Global options
Accepted by every command except
.Cm render ,
after the command name.
.Fl \-name Ns = Ns Ar value
works for options that take a value.
.Bl -tag -width "--fail-on-warning"
.It Fl \-config Ar file
Read this file instead of
.Ar dir Ns Pa /site.toml .
.It Fl \-output Ar dir
Build into
.Ar dir
instead of the configured dist.
.It Fl \-base-url Ar url
Override
.Ic base_url .
.It Fl \-verbose
One line on standard error per page and copied file.
.It Fl \-quiet , Fl q
No summary line and no notes.
.It Fl \-color Ar auto | always | never
Colour the
.Dq warning:
label.
.Ar auto
colours only a terminal, and not when
.Ev NO_COLOR
is set.
.It Fl \-json
One line of JSON on standard output (see
.Pa docs/cli.md
for its fields); messages stay on standard error.
.It Fl \-fail-on-warning
Exit 3 if any warning was printed.
.It Fl \-no-plugins
Don't start the plugins in
.Pa site.toml .
The manifest's
.Li plugins
is then empty.
.El
.Ss Build options
Options and
.Ar content-dir
may come in any order.
There is no
.Fl \-
terminator: write a directory whose name starts with
.Sq -
as
.Pa ./-dir ,
and one named
.Pa render
as
.Pa ./render .
.Bl -tag -width "--check-links"
.It Fl \-target Ar name
With
.Cm build :
also write the files that serve each page in the format the
.Li Accept
header asks for:
.Ar name
is
.Li cloudflare
.Pq Pa worker.js , wrangler.jsonc , _headers ,
.Li vercel
.Pq Pa vercel.json
or
.Li nginx
.Pq Pa nginx.ssg.conf , nginx.ssg-maps.conf .
Overrides
.Ic deploy.target .
Files that exist and differ are kept with a warning.
.It Fl \-force
With
.Fl \-target :
replace files that exist and differ.
.It Fl \-drafts
Also build pages whose
.Ic draft
key is true.
Without it, a page whose own frontmatter sets a true
.Ic draft
is not rendered at all (so a broken template in a draft does not fail the build), and a
page made a draft by a template is dropped after the first pass.
Drafts that are not built do not count when deciding between
.Pa foo.md
and
.Pa foo/index.md ;
with
.Fl \-drafts
they do, so a draft
.Pa foo/index.md
moves
.Pa foo.md
from
.Pa /foo/
to
.Pa /foo .
.It Fl \-check-links
After the build, warn about every
.Li href
or
.Li src
attribute in a page's HTML output (skeleton included) that points at nothing in dist.
See
.Sx Link checking .
Does not change the exit status.
.It Fl \-incremental
Keep dist instead of emptying it.
A file whose bytes are unchanged is not rewritten, a changed one is replaced, and files the build
no longer produces are removed, so the result equals a clean build.
Only for a dist ssg owns.
.Cm serve
and
.Cm watch
always build this way.
.It Fl \-quiet , Fl q
No summary line and no notes.
Warnings and errors still print.
.El
.Ss Render options
Options are applied left to right, so a later one overrides an earlier one:
.Li --strict --no-html
escapes raw HTML,
.Li --no-html --strict
does not.
.Bl -tag -width "--no-extensions"
.It Fl \-strict
Plain CommonMark 0.31.2: raw HTML and scripts pass through unchanged, no extensions,
no heading ids, no bare autolinks.
The same as
.Fl \-scripts \-no-extensions
plus heading ids and autolinks off.
.It Fl \-text
Write plain text instead of HTML, as in the
.Pa .txt
output, wrapped at 80 columns.
.It Fl \-no-html
Escape raw HTML so it shows as text.
.It Fl \-scripts
Turn the raw HTML allow-list off, so
.Li <script>
and similar elements,
.Li on*
event attributes and
.Li javascript: ,
.Li vbscript: ,
.Li file:
and non-image
.Li data:
URLs pass through.
.It Fl \-no-scripts
Escape tags and drop attributes that are not on the allow-list, and neutralize those URLs.
This is the default, so the flag only undoes an earlier
.Fl \-scripts
or
.Fl \-strict .
.It Fl \-no-extensions
CommonMark syntax only: no tables, strikethrough, task lists, footnotes, definition lists,
containers, alerts, marks, heading attributes or bare autolinks.
Heading ids stay on and raw HTML is still sanitized.
.El
.Pp
The width of
.Fl \-text
output and the heading ids cannot be set separately here; a site sets them in the
.Ic [markdown]
table of
.Pa site.toml .
.Ss Other options
.Fl \-version
is recognised only as the first argument; elsewhere it is an unknown option.
.Fl \-help
also works after a command.
.Bl -tag -width "--version"
.It Fl \-help , Fl h
Print usage and a summary of the options to standard output.
.It Fl \-version
Print the version and the git commit ssg was built from, as in
.Dq ssg 1.0.0-dev (abc1234) ,
to standard output.
Source builds carry the
.Dq -dev
suffix; release builds drop it.
The commit ends in
.Dq -dirty
if the tree had uncommitted changes, and is left out when it is unknown.
Later arguments are ignored.
.El
.Ss Link checking
For each page,
.Fl \-check-links
reads
.Li href
and
.Li src
values (quoted, unquoted, or with blanks around
.Sq = )
in real tags only: escaped text, HTML comments and the contents of
.Li <script>
and
.Li <style>
are not scanned.
Copied
.Pa .html
assets are not scanned.
A value is skipped if it is empty, starts with
.Sq #
or
.Sq // ,
or has a scheme
.Pq a Sq \&:
before any
.Sq / ,
.Sq \&?
or
.Sq # .
Otherwise the query and fragment are cut, basic entities and
.Li %XX
escapes are decoded, and the path is resolved against the page URL.
It exists if dist has, for
.Pa /a/ ,
the file
.Pa a/index.html ;
for
.Pa /a ,
the file
.Pa a ,
.Pa a/index.html
or
.Pa a.html .
A path that climbs above the site root is broken, and so is
.Pa .ssg-dist .
Each broken link is reported once per page.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set and not empty,
.Fl \-color Cm auto
does not colour.
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC, used for the
.Ic build_date
key instead of the current time.
With it set, the same input builds byte-identical output (apart from the summary line).
It must be a decimal integer from 0 to 253402300799 (9999-12-31T23:59:59Z); anything else
is ignored with a warning and the current time is used.
.El
.Pp
No other environment variables are read.
.Sh FILES
Paths other than
.Pa site.toml
are set in
.Pa site.toml ;
the names below are the usual ones.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa content-dir/site.toml
Site configuration.
Required.
.It Pa content-dir/skeleton.html
The HTML page every page is placed in.
.It Pa content-dir/templates/
Templates for
.Li {{extend}}
and
.Li {{include}} .
May be missing until a page uses one.
.It Pa .assetignore
In any directory: gitignore-style patterns for files not to publish.
.It Pa dist/
Output.
.It Pa dist/.ssg-dist
Marker written when
.Nm
owns dist: dist was missing, empty or already marked.
Only a marked dist is emptied.
It is published with the site.
.It Pa dist/sitemap.xml
Written when
.Ic base_url
is set, unless the content directory has its own.
.It Pa manifest.json
Written beside dist (not inside it) by
.Ic build ;
see
.Xr ssg 5 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success, including builds that printed warnings.
.It 1
An error: configuration, template, unsafe dist, or file I/O.
.It 2
Bad usage; the usage text is printed to standard error.
.It 3
Warnings were printed and
.Fl \-fail-on-warning
was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build a site and preview it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ssg mysite
ssg: built 12 pages, copied 4 files in 9 ms
$ python3 -m http.server -d mysite/dist
.Ed
.Pp
Reproducible CI build, with a builder checked out into
.Pa ./builder
inside the content directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git log -1 --format=%ct) builder/build/ssg .
ssg: note: skipping builder/ (a nested git checkout; set nested_repos = true to build it)
ssg: built 12 pages, copied 4 files in 9 ms
.Ed
.Pp
Preview drafts and look for broken links:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ssg --drafts --check-links mysite
ssg: warning: guide/a.md: broken link ../setup/
ssg: built 13 pages, copied 4 files in 11 ms (1 warning)
.Ed
.Pp
Render one file, or standard input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ssg render README.md > readme.html
$ printf '# Hi\en\enSome *text*.\en' | ssg render --text -
Hi
==

Some text.
.Ed
.Pp
Check how strict CommonMark would render a file:
.Dl $ ssg render --strict notes.md
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Everything except
.Cm render
output and
.Fl \-help
and
.Fl \-version
goes to standard error.
Errors are
.Dq ssg: Ar message ,
with the source file at fault, relative to
.Ar content-dir ,
in front where there is one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ssg: guide/a.md: missing template "post" (looked for /srv/site/templates/post.md)
.Ed
.Pp
Warnings
.Pq Dq ssg: warning: ...
and notes
.Pq Dq ssg: note: ...
do not change the exit status.
The summary line counts the warnings printed during the build; the
.Pa site.toml
warnings come before it and are not counted.
In the messages below,
.Ar src
is a full path to the file being evaluated.
.Ss Usage (exit 2)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li unknown option Ar opt
Includes
.Fl \-
and options of the other mode.
.It Ar option Li needs a value
.It Li --color wants auto, always or never
.It Li --port wants a number from 0 to 65535
.It Li plugins needs list or meta <name>
.It Li new takes one path
.It Li completions needs bash, zsh or fish
.It Li one content dir only
.It Li render takes one input
.It Li render needs a file or -
.El
.Ss site.toml (exit 1)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li missing site.toml in Ar dir
.It Li site.toml must set dist, templates, and skeleton
.It Li site.toml: Ns Ar N : Ar message
A syntax or type error on line
.Ar N ,
for example
.Li \(aqclean\(aq must be a boolean ,
.Li duplicate key \(aqdist\(aq ,
.Li duplicate table [markdown] ,
.Li \(aqa\(aq is not a table ,
.Li leading zeros are not allowed ,
.Li only integers are supported ,
.Li \(aqtext_width\(aq must be between 0 and 100000 .
See
.Xr ssg 5
for the TOML subset.
.It Li warning: site.toml: Ns Ar N : Li unknown key \(aq Ns Ar k Ns Li \(aq
Also
.Li unknown key \(aq Ns Ar k Ns Li \(aq in [markdown]
and
.Li unknown table [ Ns Ar t Ns Li \&] .
Keys inside an unknown table are ignored without further warnings.
.Li [plugin.\& Ns Ar name Ns Li \&]
tables are accepted without warnings here; each plugin checks its own keys.
.El
.Ss Dist (exit 1, nothing written)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li dist ( Ns Ar path Ns Li \&) must not be the content dir or contain it
.It Li dist ( Ns Ar path Ns Li \&) must not be or contain the templates dir
.It Li dist ( Ns Ar path Ns Li \&) must not contain the skeleton
.It Li dist ( Ns Ar path Ns Li \&) must not be inside a hidden dir ( Ns Ar part Ns Li \&)
Only the parts of dist's path below what it shares with the content directory are checked.
.El
.Ss Plugins (exit 1)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li plugin \(aq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(aq: ssg-plugin- Ns Ar name Ns Li " is not on PATH ..."
Or
.Ar path Li " is not an executable file" .
With
.Li required = false
a warning instead.
.It Li plugin \(aq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(aq: needs plugin protocol Ar N Ns Li ", but this ssg speaks 1"
Also problems with
.Fl \-meta :
it timed out, exited non-zero, printed no JSON, or names another plugin.
.It Li plugin \(aq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(aq, hook \(aq Ns Ar hook Ns Li \(aq: Ar what
.Ar what
is
.Li timed out after Ns Ar N Ns Li s ,
.Li exited before answering ,
.Li answered with invalid JSON ,
.Li answered with the wrong id ,
.Li failed: Ar message
(the plugin's own error),
.Li the result must be a string ,
or, for
.Li asset ,
.Li \(aq Ns Ar path Ns Li \(aq is not a path inside dist .
.It Li [plugin. Ns Ar name Ns Li \&] \(aq Ns Ar key Ns Li \(aq must be Ar type Ns Li ", not " Ar type
A config value of the wrong type for the plugin's
.Fl \-meta .
.It Li "warning: [plugin.name] has the key 'k', which name does not declare"
.It Li "warning: plugin name: text"
The plugin wrote
.Ar text
to standard error.
.El
.Ss Skeleton (exit 1)
Prefixed with the skeleton's path relative to
.Ar content-dir .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li missing HTML skeleton: Ar path
Not prefixed.
.It Li HTML skeleton has no <main tag
Also
.Li has a malformed <main tag
and
.Li has no </main> tag .
Not checked when the skeleton contains
.Li {{content}} .
.It Li missing {{end}} for {{if Ar key Ns Li }}
Also
.Li {{end}} without {{if}} ,
.Li {{else}} without {{if}} ,
.Li second {{else}} in one {{if}} .
.El
.Ss Pages and templates (exit 1)
Prefixed with the page's path relative to
.Ar content-dir .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li frontmatter line Ar N Ns Li : expected key: value, got: Ar line
Line 1 is the opening
.Li --- .
In a template's frontmatter, the template's path comes first.
.It Li unclosed frontmatter (missing closing ---)
.It Li missing template \(dq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(dq (looked for Ar path Ns Li \&)
For an
.Li {{include}} ,
.Li in Ar src
follows.
.It Li bad template path \(dq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(dq in Ar src Li (must be relative to the templates dir, without \(dq..\(dq)
.It Li cyclic {{extend}} in Ar src
.It Li cyclic {{include \(dq Ns Ar name Ns Li \(dq}} in Ar src Li (in include Ar path Ns Li \&)
.It Li {{extend}} inside included template Ar path Li in Ar src
.It Li missing {{end}} for {{if Ar key Ns Li }} in Ar src
Also
.Li {{end}} without {{if}} ,
.Li {{else}} without {{if}} ,
.Li second {{else}} in one {{if}} ,
each followed by
.Li in Ar src .
.It Li {{if}} nested too deeply in Ar src
More than 256 levels.
.It Li template expansion nested more than 64 levels deep in Ar src
Keys and includes nested more than 64 levels.
.It Li template expansion larger than 64 MiB in Ar src
.El
.Ss Files (exit 1)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li cannot read file: Ar path
.It Li cannot read Ar path Ns Li : is a directory
.It Li error reading file: Ar path
.It Li cannot write file: Ar path
.It Li error writing file (disk full?): Ar path
.It Li error writing output
.Cm render
could not write standard output.
.El
.Pp
Other file system failures are reported with the C++ library's message.
.Ss Build warnings
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li not cleaning Ar path Ns Li : it wasn't created by ssg (no .ssg-dist); delete it once by hand
dist is not empty and has no marker, for example output of an older
.Nm .
It is built over, never emptied, until it is deleted by hand.
Also
.Li not cleaning Ar path Ns Li : not a plain directory
when dist is a symbolic link or a file.
Neither appears with
.Li clean = false .
.It Ar a Li and Ar b Li both write Ar out Li (the latter wins)
Two sources produce the same output file, for example an asset
.Pa index.html
and the page
.Pa index.md .
Pages are written after assets, so the page wins.
.It Li sitemap.xml exists in the content dir; not generating one
.It Li ignoring SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH= Ns Ar value Li (want seconds from 0 to 253402300799); using the current time
.It Ar page Ns Li : broken link Ar link
From
.Fl \-check-links .
.Ar link
is the value from the page, decoded, without query or fragment.
.El
.Ss Notes
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li note: skipping Ar dir Ns Li / (a nested git checkout; set nested_repos = true to build it)
.Ar dir
contains a
.Pa .git
file or directory.
Not shown with
.Fl \-quiet ,
not counted as a warning.
.It Li note: skipping Ar path Li (a symlink; set follow_symlinks = true to copy what it points to)
.Ar path
is a symbolic link to a file.
Not shown with
.Fl \-quiet ,
not counted as a warning.
.It Li built Ar N Li pages, copied Ar M Li files in Ar T Li ms ( Ns Ar K Li warnings)
The summary line.
The part in parentheses only appears when there were warnings.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssg 5
.Pp
In the source tree:
.Pa docs/cli.md ,
.Pa docs/configuration.md ,
.Pa docs/templates.md ,
.Pa docs/markdown.md ,
.Pa docs/getting-started.md .
.Sh STANDARDS
.Cm render
.Fl \-strict
passes all 652 examples of the CommonMark 0.31.2 specification.
.Sh CAVEATS
A dist directory made by an
.Nm
older than the
.Pa .ssg-dist
marker is never emptied; delete it once.
.Pp
.Pa .ssg-dist
is deployed with the site unless the deploy step excludes it.
